==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|dyew}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*Tīwaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*deywós||god}}.

Proto-Germanic cognate with Old Norse {{term|Týr|lang=non}}, Old Frisian {{term|Tii|lang=ofs}}, Old High German [[Zio|Zīo]], Gothic [[𐍄𐌴𐌹𐍅𐍃]].

Proto-Indo-European cognate with Ancient Greek {{term|Ζεύς|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|Iovis|lang=la}}, Hittite {{term|sc=Xsux|𒅆𒍑|tr=sius|lang=hit}}, Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*divъ}} (Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|дивъ|tr=divŭ|lang=cu}}), Sanskrit {{term|द्यु |tr=dyú|sc=Deva|lang=sa}}.

